{"experiments":{"tracks":[{"id":"compass","name":"Compass","kind":"main","since":"2026-09-08","blurb":"The line behind every live issue since the first day. Each version has to pass a fixed gate on held-out days before it is adopted, and the version that made every hour's forecast is on the record.","version":"v0.10","issues":["a1","spot","a2"],"n_days":10,"series":["power_price_SE1","power_price_SE2","power_price_SE3","power_price_SE4"]},{"id":"echo","name":"Echo","kind":"shadow","since":"2026-09-12","blurb":"A second way of ordering the hours of the day, run beside Compass on the spot series. It keeps Compass's price levels and only re-orders the hours, so any difference is about which hours are cheap, not how cheap.","version":"v0.1","issues":["spot"],"n_days":3,"series":["power_price_SE1","power_price_SE2","power_price_SE3","power_price_SE4"]},{"id":"scout","name":"Scout","kind":"shadow","since":"2026-09-15","blurb":"Built on a different principle from Compass: it reasons about the coming day in words and writes down why, rather than fitting a curve to the past. Run on every issue beside Compass and scored on the same hours.","version":"v0.1","issues":["a1","spot","a2"],"n_days":0,"series":[]}],"main":"compass","series":{"power_price_SE1":{"name":"Spot SE1","unit":"SEK/MWh","tracks":{"echo":{"n":3,"version":"v0.1","mae":430.065789557563,"mae_main":426.46941713121197,"mae_naive":523.1698269971212,"skill":0.17796140494943047,"skill_main":0.18483560189422255,"spearman":0.5985507246376811,"spearman_main":0.7026086956521738,"top4":0.5,"top4_main":0.5833333333333334,"main_versions":["v0.9"]}},"days":[{"target_date":"2026-09-15","issue":"spot","track":"echo","version":"v0.1","main_version":"v0.9","hours_realised":24,"mae":493.1989121500651,"mae_main":493.1989121500651,"mae_naive":239.84677055358884},{"target_date":"2026-09-14","issue":"spot","track":"echo","version":"v0.1","main_version":"v0.9","hours_realised":24,"mae":703.9912015787762,"mae_main":697.633253885905,"ma